{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 35, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Tripoli and ruled the County of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem.\n\n**Early Life and Succession**\nRaymond III succeeded his father as the Count of Tripoli in 1152 at the age of 20. His early years in power were marked by conflicts with the Muslim states of the region particularly with Nur ad-Din Zangi who had recently conquered Aleppo and Damascus. \n\nHe married Eschiva of Byblos in 1152 however the marriage was childless. After Eschiva's death in 1168 he married Stephanie of Milly and they had a son Raymond IV Count of Tripoli.\n\n**Military Campaigns**\nRaymond III played a significant role in the Second Crusade led by King Louis VII of France and Emperor Conrad III of the Holy Roman Empire in 1147. He was instrumental in the capture of the port city of Ascalon from the Fatimids but the city was returned to the Fatimids after a short period of time.\n\nIn 1160 Raymond III allied with the Holy Roman Empire and launched a joint campaign against the County of Edessa which was being threatened by the Seljuk Turks. The campaign was unsuccessful and the County of Edessa was eventually captured by the Seljuk Turks in 1164.\n\n**Later Life and Death**\nRaymond III died in 1187 without an heir. His son Raymond IV was still a minor and the County of Tripoli was placed under the regency of Bohemond III Prince of Antioch. The County of Tripoli was eventually captured by the Ayyubid Sultan Saladin in 1188.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.014390614}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.00016938205}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0010648064}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1300828}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.349725e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00021371941}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -6.651657